---
layout: model.njk
title: "Ten essays, each tied to a layer."
name: "Essays"
description: "A ten-part series on the AI-native organisation: workflow, org design, governance and the context layer, plus shorter notes."
---
<section class="m-sec">
  <span class="m-eyebrow">Series · The AI-native organisation</span>
  <h1>Ten essays, each tied to a layer.</h1>
  <p class="m-lede">The layer pages show the pattern. The essays work through the mechanism. New essays arrive here first, then on LinkedIn.</p>
  <div class="m-filter" role="group" aria-label="Filter by layer" data-essay-filter>
    <button type="button" class="m-chip" data-filter="all" aria-pressed="true">All</button>
    {% for key in ["workflow", "org", "governance", "context"] %}{% set l = layers | byKey(key) %}<button type="button" class="m-chip" data-filter="{{ l.key }}" aria-pressed="false">{{ l.name }}</button>{% endfor %}
  </div>
  <div data-essay-list>{% set list = series %}{% include "partials/essay-list.njk" %}</div>
</section>

<section class="m-sec" id="notes">
  <h2>Notes</h2>
  <p class="m-small">Shorter pieces and working models, outside the series.</p>
  <ul class="m-notes">
    {% for note in collections.notes %}
    <li><a href="{{ note.url }}"><b>{{ note.data.title }}</b><span>{{ note.data.year }}{% if note.data.type %} · {{ note.data.type }}{% endif %}{% if note.data.excerpt %} · {{ note.data.excerpt }}{% endif %}</span></a></li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>
